          "lineage": "Solaropsis",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "of radula (MNRJ 23832) Formula 25 - 32 - 1 - 32 - 25; central tooth monocuspid, triangular-lanceolate, with sharp serrated edges, up to 56 µm long; lateral teeth very similar to the central tooth (but slightly narrower), monocuspid, triangular-lanceolate, with sharp serrated edges (mainly in inner lateral teeth; smooth edges in outer lateral teeth), up to 57 µm (L 1) or 51 µm (L 32) long; marginal teeth bicuspid, smooth edges; inner marginal teeth up 48 µm long (M 1), with elongated, lanceolate mesocone, 2.5 – 2.7 x longer than ectocone; outer marginal teeth up 27 µm long (M 24), short, triangular mesocone, 1.3 – 1.4 x longer than ectocone.",
